# Environment config. Vite loads .env, .env.local, .env.[mode] and .env.[mode].local, so
# `.env.*` is needed — only the exact name `.env` was ignored before, leaving
# .env.production (the file most likely to hold real production values) committable.
# The negation keeps the placeholders-only template tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

package-lock.json
yarn.lock
package.json
.gitignore